<h2>Your television</h2>
<p>Any HDMI television works. A Full HD set looks good from a sofa. To see the game at its best you want 4K, HDR with real brightness (600 nits or more), and a game mode with low delay. A 120Hz panel is not needed for this game, though it helps others. If the picture looks grey, turn HDR off on cheap sets: a good SDR picture beats a weak HDR one. Browse <a href="/products?category=tv">televisions</a> and <a href="/products?category=monitor">monitors</a>.</p>

<h2>Power and heat</h2>
<p>A PS5 uses around 200 watts in demanding games. A UPS of 1,000VA keeps the console, router and television on long enough to save. Give the console ten centimetres of air on each side, keep it out of closed cabinets and clean the vents every couple of months. In the monsoon, run it every few days.</p>

