<h2>Mistakes people are making</h2>
<ul>
<li>Paying extra for a disc console to play a game without a disc.</li>
<li>Buying a "secondary" account for Rs 4,000 and losing it.</li>
<li>Using a code from another region.</li>
<li>Buying a Series S because it is small and cheap, and placing it under a 65-inch screen.</li>
<li>Downloading a "GTA 6 APK" or "PC repack".</li>
<li>Filling the console to the last gigabyte, so the first patch fails.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Should you wait?</h2>
<p>If you have a console, no. If you must buy one, think about the next year. Prices have been rising, GTA VI has increased demand, and nothing suggests a fall soon. PC owners with a strong machine may prefer to wait for an announcement. And if your interest is mainly online play with friends, there is no online mode yet, so there is no hurry.</p>

<h2>Our recommendation</h2>
<p>For most homes in Nepal: a PlayStation 5 Digital Edition, the Standard Edition of the game from your own account, an Ethernet cable and a small UPS. Add an NVMe drive when the space runs out. If you own or plan a large 4K television, and the price gap stays small, go straight to the Pro. Then close the door for a weekend, after the dishes are done.</p>
