<tr><td>1999</td><td>GTA 2</td><td>Anywhere City</td><td>PC, PlayStation, Dreamcast</td></tr>
<tr><td>2001</td><td>GTA III</td><td>Liberty City</td><td>PlayStation 2</td></tr>
<tr><td>2002</td><td>GTA: Vice City</td><td>Vice City, 1986</td><td>PlayStation 2</td></tr>
<tr><td>2004</td><td>GTA: San Andreas</td><td>San Andreas, 1992</td><td>PlayStation 2</td></tr>
<tr><td>2004</td><td>GTA Advance</td><td>Liberty City</td><td>Game Boy Advance</td></tr>
<tr><td>2005</td><td>Liberty City Stories</td><td>Liberty City, 1998</td><td>PSP</td></tr>
<tr><td>2006</td><td>Vice City Stories</td><td>Vice City, 1984</td><td>PSP</td></tr>
<tr><td>2008</td><td>GTA IV</td><td>Liberty City</td><td>PS3, Xbox 360</td></tr>
<tr><td>2009</td><td>The Lost and Damned; The Ballad of Gay Tony</td><td>Liberty City</td><td>Xbox 360</td></tr>
<tr><td>2009</td><td>Chinatown Wars</td><td>Liberty City</td><td>Nintendo DS</td></tr>
<tr><td>2013</td><td>GTA V and GTA Online</td><td>Los Santos and Blaine County</td><td>PS3, Xbox 360</td></tr>
<tr><td>2021</td><td>The Trilogy – The Definitive Edition</td><td>Remasters of III, Vice City, San Andreas</td><td>Consoles, PC</td></tr>
<tr><td>2026</td><td>GTA VI</td><td>Leonida and Vice City, present day</td><td>PS5, Xbox Series X|S</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>Fans sort these into three families: the 2D games of the 1990s, the 3D games of the PlayStation 2 era, and the HD games from GTA IV onwards. City names return, but each family is its own world.</p>

<h2>1997: a game seen from above</h2>
<p>The first Grand Theft Auto came from DMA Design, the studio that had made Lemmings. Programmers David Jones and Mike Dailly led a team that had started with a racing game about police and criminals, and found that playing the criminal was more fun. You answered pay phones, stole cars and finished jobs for points in three cities. It looked simple. The idea underneath was not: a city that carries on whether or not you are doing a mission.</p>
<p>Newspapers were outraged, and that was partly the plan. The controversy sold copies. GTA 2 followed in 1999 with rival gangs whose respect you could win or lose, set in a strange near future.</p>

<h2>2001: GTA III changes everything</h2>
<p>DMA became Rockstar North, under brothers Sam and Dan Houser. GTA III took the same idea and put the camera behind the player, in a three-dimensional Liberty City. You could drive, walk, shoot, listen to radio stations, take a taxi fare or simply watch the rain. Nothing like it had existed at that scale, and within a few years half the industry was making "GTA clones". The modern open-world game begins here.</p>
<p>It arrived in October 2001, after changes made in the wake of the attacks in New York, and became one of the defining games of the PlayStation 2.</p>

<h2>2002: Vice City and the 1980s</h2>
<p>One year later came neon, pastel suits and a soundtrack people still hum. Vice City was set in 1986 and had a hero who spoke: Tommy Vercetti, voiced by Ray Liotta. You could buy businesses and build an empire. For many Nepalis it was the first GTA they played, installed from a copied disc on a computer that barely ran it, with cheat codes written on the back of a notebook. PANZER and LEAVEMEALONE needed no internet.</p>

<h2>2004: San Andreas, the biggest of its age</h2>
<p>San Andreas gave players a whole state with three cities, countryside, desert and a mountain. Its hero, CJ, could get fat or muscular, change his hair, learn fighting styles, swim, fly jets and date. Set in the early 1990s, it drew on hip-hop, gang films and the riots in Los Angeles. It became the best-selling game on the PlayStation 2.</p>
<p>It also produced the "Hot Coffee" scandal, when hidden sexual content was unlocked by modders. The game was re-rated, pulled from shelves and patched. American politicians called hearings. Rockstar learned to be more careful about what stayed on the disc.</p>

<h2>2005 to 2009: handhelds</h2>
<p>Rockstar put full 3D cities on Sony's PSP with Liberty City Stories and Vice City Stories, both prequels. Chinatown Wars, made for the Nintendo DS, returned to a high camera and used the touch screen for hot-wiring cars and trading. It was among the best-reviewed games on the machine and sold less than it deserved.</p>

<h2>2008: GTA IV grows up</h2>
<p>A new generation of consoles brought a new tone. Niko Bellic, a veteran from Eastern Europe, came to Liberty City for a dream his cousin had exaggerated. The city was the most detailed yet, cars had weight, and bodies obeyed physics in a way that was often funny. It dropped some of the toys of San Andreas and gained a sadder, more adult story, as well as online multiplayer for the first time. Two expansions told other people's versions of the same weeks.</p>
<p>It made several hundred million dollars in its first week, a record then, and divided fans. Some missed the jets. Some think that it has the best writing in the series.</p>

<h2>2013: GTA V and the game that never ended</h2>
<p>GTA V had three leads, Michael, Franklin and Trevor, and let you switch between them in an instant. Los Santos was a portrait of Los Angeles with mountains and a desert behind it. Heists were planned, crews were chosen, and things went wrong in different ways. It earned more than $800 million on its first day and passed a billion in three, faster than any entertainment product before it.</p>
<p>Two weeks later came GTA Online. It was broken at first, and it grew into a second life for tens of millions: races, robberies, businesses, role-play servers and an economy of its own. GTA V was released again for PS4 and Xbox One in 2014, for PC in 2015, and for PS5 and Xbox Series in 2022. Take-Two says that it has sold more than 230 million copies, making it one of the best-selling games of any kind.</p>
<p>In Nepal the PC version is the one people know, through cyber cafes, mods, YouTube channels and role-play streams in Nepali.</p>

<h2>2013 to 2023: the long silence</h2>
<p>Rockstar's next release was Red Dead Redemption 2 in 2018, a Western of extraordinary detail that took much of the company's strength. Early work on the next GTA had begun years before, and full production followed. Dan Houser, co-writer of most of the series, left in 2020.</p>
<p>In 2021 remasters of the three PlayStation 2 classics arrived in poor condition and were apologised for and patched. In February 2022 Rockstar confirmed what everyone knew, that a new GTA was in development. That September, a teenager broke into the company's systems and published ninety videos of unfinished work, one of the largest leaks the industry has seen.</p>

<h2>2023 to 2026: the road to GTA VI</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>December 2023:</strong> The first trailer is released a day early after a leak. It passes a hundred million views within two days. Vice City, Lucia and Jason are shown, with a date of 2025.</li>
<li><strong>May 2025:</strong> The game is delayed to 26 May 2026. A second trailer follows days later and breaks viewing records again.</li>
<li><strong>November 2025:</strong> A second delay, to 19 November 2026, for polish.</li>
<li><strong>June 2026:</strong> Editions and prices are announced. Boxed copies will contain a code and no disc, which angers collectors. Pre-orders open.</li>
<li><strong>August 2026:</strong> More leaks. Rockstar confirms 30 frames per second on all consoles. An extended look is shown on Netflix.</li>
<li><strong>19 November 2026:</strong> Release on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What happened on release day</h2>
<p>Offices emptied. Internet providers reported their busiest days. Take-Two announced 32.5 million copies sold before launch and $3.79 billion in sales on the first day, almost five times the opening of GTA V. Critics gave it some of the highest scores ever printed. Complaints were about the 30 frame limit, controls, the lack of a disc and the absence of an online mode.</p>
<p>What stands out in the reviews is tone. The satire remains, aimed at social media, police, money and fame, while the centre is a relationship between two people in trouble. Lucia is the first woman to lead a main game in the series.</p>

<h2>What each game added</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Game</th><th>The idea it gave to others</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Grand Theft Auto</td><td>Freedom to ignore the mission</td></tr>
<tr><td>GTA 2</td><td>Gangs that remember you</td></tr>
<tr><td>GTA III</td><td>A living 3D city</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vice City</td><td>A strong period mood, licensed music, property</td></tr>
<tr><td>San Andreas</td><td>A whole state, and a character who changes</td></tr>
<tr><td>GTA IV</td><td>Physical weight, a serious story</td></tr>
<tr><td>GTA V</td><td>Several leads, heists, a permanent online world</td></tr>
<tr><td>GTA VI</td><td>Crowds that react, a relationship at the core</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h2>Why it has always been controversial</h2>
<p>Every main GTA has been blamed for something. Courts and researchers have generally not found that games turn people violent, and the series is plainly made for adults, with age ratings to match. It is also fair to say that many children have played it. Parents who remember Vice City fondly might think about the age at which they played it, and use the controls that today's consoles offer.</p>

<h2>How to play the old ones today</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>GTA III, Vice City and San Andreas:</strong> The Definitive Edition on modern consoles, PC, Android and iPhone.</li>
<li><strong>GTA IV:</strong> The Complete Edition on PC, and on Xbox through backward compatibility.</li>
<li><strong>GTA V and Online:</strong> PS4, PS5, Xbox One, Xbox Series and PC. Often on sale for very little.</li>
<li><strong>Chinatown Wars and Liberty City Stories:</strong> Mobile.</li>
</ul>
<p>An ordinary laptop with integrated graphics runs everything up to GTA IV at modest settings. A <a href="/guides/best-gaming-laptops-nepal">gaming laptop</a> is needed for GTA V with mods.</p>

<h2>What comes next</h2>
<p>An online mode for GTA VI has not been dated, and neither has a PC version. History suggests that both will come. History also suggests patience: the gap between the last two games was thirteen years. If the next one takes as long, it will arrive around 2039, and some of the children being told that they are too young for this one will be reviewing it.</p>
<p>If you are ready to play now, see the <a href="/products/gta-6">GTA VI page</a> for editions and prices in Nepal and our guide to <a href="/guides/how-to-play-gta-6-nepal-consoles">the console you need</a>.</p>
